{"wall_time": "2026-09-16T16:24:11+0500", "elapsed_seconds": 203.281, "event": "box8_answer", "question": "What happens after the capture?", "answer": {"answer": "the image is converted to grayscale", "quote": "After capture, the image is converted to grayscale and corrected only when the correction improves measured recognition Excessive sharpening can create bright halos around letters, while aggressive thresholding can erase punctuation and thin strokes For that reason several preprocessing alternatives are tested on the same stored photographs The comparison includes raw grayscale.", "region_id": 4, "bbox": [515, 654, 1252, 934], "table": null, "row": null, "margin": 18.430503129959106, "score": 0.9999999900977431, "source_text": "After capture, the image is converted to grayscale and corrected only when the correction improves measured recognition Excessive sharpening can create bright halos around letters, while aggressive thresholding can erase punctuation and thin strokes For that reason several preprocessing alternatives are tested on the same stored photographs The comparison includes raw grayscale. local contrast enhancement, mild gamma correction, edge-preserving filtering and adaptive binarization Each alternative is evaluated using character count, recognition confidence, focus statistics, and processing time Ground-truth text is retained for important experiments so that character error rate and word error rate can be calculated instead of relying on confidence alone", "translated": false, "model_device": "cuda"}}
